ude through MCP (Model Context Protocol):\n\n## MCP Servers for Bitwig Studio & Claude\n\nThere is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for Bitwig Studio, enabling Claude to control your DAW. There are multiple projects implementing this integration:\n\n### WigAI\nWigAI is a Model Context Protocol (MCP) server implemented as a Bitwig Studio extension that provides an interface for external AI assistants to control Bitwig Studio through simple text-based commands. It requires Bitwig Studio (5.2.7 or later), Java 21 LTS, and an external AI agent that supports the Model Context Protocol.\n\n### Bitwig MCP Server (WeModulate)\nA Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for Bitwig Studio allows Claude to control your DAW. It translates between MCP requests from Claude and OSC commands to Bitwig Studio's control API.\n\n## Capabilities\n\nThese systems enable transport control (play, stop, set beats), mixer control (adjust volume, pan, mute/unmute tracks), device control (manipulate device parameters), access to project information (track and device information), and templates/prompts for common tasks.\n\n## Bitwig's Native APIs\nBitwig has a JavaScript API and a Java API for fancy controller mapping.\n\nThese projects represent ongoing development efforts (as of 2025-2026) to enable hands-free, AI-driven music production workflows in Bitwig Studio using Claude and the Model Context Protocol.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"c350e642-dbab-4483-a0cb-f2e5093e5d0e","timestamp":"2026-05-26T00:06:39.266Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Bitwig Studio Controller API Java JavaScript automation MCP Claude 2026","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01DU5VmsMADZPp5aQPYjjQWM","content":[{"title":"Bitwig MCP Server - The Key Tool for MCP Integration to Enable Claude AI to Control Bitwig Studio","url":"https://mcp.aibase.com/server/1916355322905075713"},{"title":"claude code and Bitwig music production","url":"h