{"parentUuid":"aeaade3c-df49-49aa-8d0b-4f5fc4605a7a","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e848e54a-7409-48b3-99ef-b08880eadfb6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ToYZgRnMbtVCaN3AKN595i","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Anticipatory Music Transformer MuseNet MIDI infill 2026 controllable composition\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Anticipatory Music Transformer: A Controllable\",\"url\":\"https://crfm.stanford.edu/2023/06/16/anticipatory-music-transformer.html\"},{\"title\":\"Stanford CRFM\",\"url\":\"https://crfm.stanford.edu/2023/06/16/anticipatory-music-transformer.html?idx=1\"},{\"title\":\"Anticipatory Music Transformer\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2306.08620\"},{\"title\":\"Anticipatory Music Transformer\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2306.08620v2\"},{\"title\":\"[2306.08620] Anticipatory Music Transformer\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.08620\"},{\"title\":\"MIDI-GPT: A Controllable Generative Model for Computer-Assisted Multitrack Music Composition\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2501.17011v1\"},{\"title\":\"Anticipatory Music Transformer | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=EBNJ33Fcrl\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Anticipatory Music Transformer\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/371605312_Anticipatory_Music_Transformer\"},{\"title\":\"Anticipatory Music Transformer - ADS\",\"url\":\"https://ui.adsabs.harvard.edu/abs/arXiv:2306.08620\"},{\"title\":\"MIDI-GPT: A Controllable Generative Model for Computer-Assisted   Multitrack Music Composition\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2501.17011\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found about the Anticipatory Music Transformer:\n\n## Overview\n\nThe Anticipatory Music Transformer is a controllable generative model that facilitates co-composition of music with AI. It is built using the generative pretrained Transformer architecture (GPT) that powers language models like GPT-4 and tools like ChatGPT.\n\n## Key Difference from Previous Models\n\nPrevious GPT-powered music models--including Google's Music Transformer and OpenAI's MuseNet--are trained to predict the next note in a sequence given the past. However, the Anticipatory Music Transformer is trained to infill parts of a pre-existing draft composition, rather than generating linearly from start to finish.\n\n## MIDI Infill and Controllable Composition\n\nThe model focuses on infilling control tasks, whereby the controls are a subset of the events themselves, and conditional generation completes a sequence of events given the fixed control events. It was trained using the large and diverse Lakh MIDI music dataset.\n\nUsers can control this model by writing parts of a musical composition, and asking the model to fill in the rest. For example, you can write a melody and ask the model to suggest accompaniments to this melody.\n\n## Performance\n\nThese models match the performance of autoregressive models for prompted generation, with the additional capability to perform infilling control tasks, including accompaniment.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"fd3ab1de-1214-4973-9fcb-393fa3d7615a","timestamp":"2026-05-26T00:06:39.819Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Anticipatory Music Transformer MuseNet MIDI infill 2026 controllable composition","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01MRnwRZj1QzjAr1W3fmFhFY","content":[{"title":"Anticipatory Music Transformer: A Controllable","url":"https://crfm.stanford.edu/2023/06/16/anticipatory-music-transformer.html"},{"title":"Stanford CRFM","url":"https://crfm.stanford.edu/2023/06/16/anticipatory-music-transformer.html?idx=1"},{"title":"Anticipatory Music Transformer","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2306.08620"},{"title":"Anticipatory Music Transformer","url":"https://arxiv.org/html/2306.08620v2"},{"title":"[2306.08620] Anticipatory Music Transformer","url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2306.08620"},{"title"