.\n\n## Sound Design and AI Technology\n\nFor the Chainsaw Man soundtrack specifically, Ushio collaborated with Sony Computer Science Laboratories to create a custom program as he sought to combine drum patterns with chainsaw samples. This tool, called ChainsawGAN, was developed specifically for the anime. While a variety of elements are included in a single piece of music, the frightening metallic roar of a chainsaw stands out with just a single sound, and Ushio considers himself a composer of sounds rather than melodies, chords, or rhythms.\n\n## Production Approach for the Reze Arc Movie\n\nFor the movie, Ushio wanted to use a full orchestra extensively, thinking it would be best to use a large orchestra in an environment capable of properly reproducing everything from soft to loud sounds.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"cf24546d-724d-40dc-8e00-f010ba5e986f","timestamp":"2026-05-26T00:08:07.605Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Kensuke Ushio Chainsaw Man A Silent Voice DAW workflow technique sound design","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_014DQX5qWNEzJmTQcV8nh3bC","content":[{"title":"How to achieve this sound? Chainsaw man/Kensuke Ushio - Gearspace","url":"https://gearspace.com/board/electronic-music-instruments-and-electronic-music-production/1427948-how-achieve-sound-chainsaw-man-kensuke-ushio.html"},{"title":"Kensuke Ushio | Composer, Music Department, Soundtrack","url":"https://www.imdb.com/name/nm7086840/"},{"title":"Composer Kensuke Ushio Interview: Chainsaw Man Anime","url":"https://screenrant.com/chainsaw-man-anime-composer-kensuke-ushio-interview/"},{"title":"Kensuke Ushio Dove Deep Creating The Emotionally Devastating Score For Chainsaw Man – The Movie: Reze Arc","url":"https://aftermath.site/kensuke-ushio-chainsaw-man-the-movie-reze-arc-score-soundtrack-interview/"},{"title":"Interview - The potential of the AI developed for Ushio Kensuke’s Chainsaw Man soundtrack​ - Music Team at Sony CSL Paris","url":"https://cslmusicteam.sony.fr/news/interview-chainsawgan-sonycsl/"},{"title":"Kensuke Ushio - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kensuke_Ushio"}]},"I found search results related to your query about Kensuke Ushio. Here are some key findings:\n\n## Background on Kensuke Ushio\n\nKensuke Ushio is known for Dandadan (2024), Chainsaw Man - The Movie: Reze Arc (2025) and A Silent Voice: The Movie (2016).\n\n## Compositional Approach and Workflow\n\nIn creative terms, there's not really that big of a distinction between the lighter sounds and the techno-based material. The workflow for how he composes them is the same. He considers himself as a composer of sounds rather than melodies, chords, or rhythms.\n\n## Sound Design and AI Technology\n\nFor the Chainsaw Man soundtrack specifically, Ushio collaborated with Sony Computer Science Laboratories to create a custom program as he sought to combine drum patterns with chainsaw samples. This tool, called ChainsawGAN, was developed specifically for the anime. While a variety of elements are included in a single piece of music, the frightening metallic roar of a chainsaw stands out with just a single sound, and Ushio considers himself a composer of sounds rather than melodies, chords, or rhythms.\n\n## Production Approach for the Reze Arc Movie\n\nFor the movie, Ushio wanted to use a full orchestra extensively, thinking it would be best to use a large orchestra in an environment capable of properly reproducing everything from soft to loud sounds."],"durationSeconds":7.521327249999973,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0cd41858-1701-42b6-a73d-13c0197fa422","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"/Users/zenray/Create/Build/Memory","sessionId":"64a2be31-6389-4261-9955-ab835d44691d","version":"2.1.149","gitBranch":"main"}
