 Max/MSP, Pure Data, MCP, and Claude code integration for natural language patch generation:\n\n## Max/MSP Integration\n\nMaxMCP is a native C++ external object for Max/MSP that acts as an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server and enables Claude Code to control Max/MSP patches through natural language commands, with zero configuration required from users.\n\nMaxMCP includes automatic patch detection with auto-generated patch IDs, natural language control, multi-patch support, a complete MCP toolset with 26 tools for comprehensive patch control, and auto-cleanup with lifecycle management on patch close.\n\nMaxPyLang (from Barnard's Programming Languages Lab) added support for generating Max MSP and Jitter patches with natural language prompts, where you describe what you want the patch to do, it generates the structure, and you can keep prompting to iterate on it in real time.\n\n## Pure Data Integration\n\nThe Pd-MCP-Server project provides integration between Claude AI and Pure Data through the Model Context Protocol (MCP), with Claude able to dynamically create, modify, and control Pure Data patches through natural language.\n\nThe Pure Data MCP Server allows you to interact with Pure Data through natural language to dynamically create, modify, and control audio processing modules, with users sending instructions to the MCP server via Claude AI and the server converting these into operation commands passed to Pure Data.\n\n## General MCP Server Capabilities\n\nMaxMSP-MCP-Server is an MCP server that integrates the Model Context Protocol with Max/MSP/Jitter, allowing large language models to directly interpret, explain, and generate Max patches with access to patch objects, subpatches, and official documentation.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"48de90f2-7b4f-4db0-ba12-caf36121ba2e","timestamp":"2026-05-26T00:08:39.420Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"Max MSP Pure Data MCP Claude code nat